"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
3015,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qaysi, narrated to us Muhammad — meaning Ibn Bakr al-Bursani — who informed us Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to 'Ata': ""I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'You were only commanded to perform Tawaf, and you were not commanded to enter it.'""

He (i.e., 'Ata') said: ""There was no prohibition against entering it, but I heard him say: 'Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that when the Prophet (ﷺ) entered the House (Ka'bah), when he came out, he prayed two rak'ahs facing the House and said: ""This is the Qiblah.""'""

**CHAPTER:**"
